nt JWT token expiration validation and automatic refresh token mechanism. Check token exp claim before making requests and refresh proactively.\",\n    \"CRITICAL: Add CSRF protection using SameSite=Strict cookies and anti-CSRF tokens in state-changing requests (POST, PUT, DELETE).\",\n    \"HIGH: Implement request timeouts on all fetch calls (recommend 30-60 seconds). Add AbortController to cancel long-running requests.\",\n    \"HIGH: Enforce HTTPS in production. Validate that API_BASE uses https:// in non-development environments. Add HSTS headers from backend.\",\n    \"HIGH: Sanitize and limit error messages exposed to users. Remove infrastructure details (URLs, port numbers, service names) from frontend error handling. Log detailed errors server-side only.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Validate Content-Type header on all API responses before parsing JSON. Reject responses with unexpected content types.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Implement Content Security Policy (CSP) headers to mitigate XSS attacks. Use nonce-based inline scripts and restrict external script sources.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Remove URL validation bypass in apiUrl() function. Only allow relative paths or validate against a whitelist of allowed base URLs.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Encrypt sensitive cached data in localStorage using a client-side encryption library. Consider using sessionStorage for sensitive temporary data instead.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Implement security headers validation. Check for X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, Strict-Transport-Security in responses.\",\n    \"LOW: Add request logging with correlation IDs but ensure sensitive data (tokens, passwords) are never logged client-side.\",\n    \"LOW: Implement rate limiting on authentication endpoints to prevent brute force attacks (client-side prevalidation + server-side enforcement).\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nThe analysis identified **11 vulnerabilities** across the frontend codebase with a **risk score of 68/100**:\n\n**Critical Issues:**\n- **Token 